  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.get_predecessors - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.get_predecessors.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.get_predecessors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get direct predecessors of a node (incoming neighbors).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.get_predecessors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get direct predecessors of a node (incoming neighbors).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.get_predecessors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get direct predecessors of a node (incoming neighbors).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet direct predecessors of a node (incoming neighbors).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L29059-L29155){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.get_predecessors(node)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Predecessors](../assets/graphs/get-predecessors.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A seven-node directed graph with the query node C outlined. The two edges pointing into C and their sources, A and E, are in the accent color; B and D are targets of C, not predecessors. The card lists A, E.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReturns the nodes that have an edge pointing *into* the specified node, i.e., every `u`\nfor which an edge `u -> node` exists. This is a thin wrapper around\n`neighbors(node, mode=\"in\")` that refuses to run on undirected graphs, where \"incoming\"\nhas no meaning.\n\nPredecessors answer \"what feeds into this node?\", which is useful for:\n\n- tracing the direct dependencies of a task in a dependency or build graph\n- finding who cites, follows, or links to a given node\n- walking a DAG backwards one step at a time (see `trav_in()` for doing this on a\n  selection)\n\nOnly one hop is examined; use `select_nodes_in_neighborhood(mode=\"in\")` for multi-hop\nupstream sets. The result is a list of node IDs (not labels) and the selection is not\nchanged.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[node]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node whose predecessors are wanted, given as an integer node ID or a string label.\n    An unknown label raises `ValueError`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Node IDs of all nodes with an edge pointing to `node=`. Empty if the node has no\n    incoming edges. Each predecessor appears once even if there are parallel edges, and\n    the order follows the internal edge order rather than being sorted.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected, or if `node=` is an ID or label not found in the graph.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~get_successors`) \n\n:   The nodes a node's edges point to.\n\n[](`~ancestors`) \n\n:   Every node with a path to a node, not just the direct predecessors.\n\n[](`~get_in_degree`) \n\n:   The number of edges pointing to a node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe predecessors of a node are the nodes with an edge pointing to it. Both \"A\" and \"B\"\npoint to \"C\", while \"D\" is pointed to by \"C\", so it isn't one:\n\n::: {#695c2742 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")], directed=True\n)\n\n[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in graph.get_predecessors(\"C\")]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['A', 'B']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### What to take first\n\nIn a prerequisite graph, each edge runs from a course to a course that requires it, so the\npredecessors of a course are its prerequisites. CS360 needs CS201 and STAT201:\n\n::: {#324b5048 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses = ec.courses()\nbefore = courses.get_predecessors(\"CS360\")\n\n[courses.get_label_from_id(n) for n in before]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['CS201', 'STAT201']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThose are only the direct prerequisites. CS201 and STAT201 have their own, and all the\ncourses that come before CS360 are its ancestors, 8 in total:\n\n::: {#08b72d26 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsorted(courses.get_label_from_id(n) for n in courses.ancestors(\"CS360\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n['CS101',\n 'CS102',\n 'CS201',\n 'MATH101',\n 'MATH102',\n 'MATH150',\n 'MATH210',\n 'STAT201']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe courses are laid out by level, from 100 at the bottom to 400 at the top. CS360 is in the\naccent color, its prerequisites in the soft one:\n\n::: {#254da56d .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses.layout_multipartite(subset_key=\"level\", align=\"horizontal\")\ncourses.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"label\",\n    highlight={\"accent\": [\"CS360\"], \"soft\": before},\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b